{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01960",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 6.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Doctor, if you're free, we can start. I've got the numbers noted down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.75,
      "end_seconds": 11.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.43,
      "end_seconds": 18.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "I wanted to get tingling in my thumb and first fingers looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 19.23,
      "end_seconds": 26.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. BP is 125 over 76, heart rate 72, respiratory rate 18, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.58,
      "end_seconds": 32.55,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.6,
      "end_seconds": 45.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "So, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.89,
      "end_seconds": 50.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "It's been like this since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.14,
      "end_seconds": 53.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.66,
      "end_seconds": 60.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "I get some relief from shaking the hand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.64,
      "end_seconds": 65.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.9,
      "end_seconds": 72.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I'd say once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.1,
      "end_seconds": 79.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 79.45,
      "end_seconds": 85.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.45,
      "end_seconds": 88.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.84,
      "end_seconds": 101.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.37,
      "text": "As for dropping things, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.51,
      "end_seconds": 109.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Have you had tingling in your thumb and first fingers before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.09,
      "end_seconds": 116.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.47,
      "end_seconds": 134.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Nothing like pain in the shoulder?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.9,
      "end_seconds": 141.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any pain in the shoulder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.53,
      "end_seconds": 147.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "A few quick ones: neck pain or weakness in the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.49,
      "end_seconds": 163.52,
      "duration_seconds": 15.03,
      "text": "No, no neck pain, no weakness in the legs. I was waking at night with numb hands at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.39,
      "end_seconds": 168.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.63,
      "end_seconds": 171.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.14,
      "end_seconds": 175.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.27,
      "end_seconds": 191.41,
      "duration_seconds": 15.14,
      "text": "I'm on Eltroxin, 100 micrograms, every morning. I do miss it now and then, to be fair. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.52,
      "end_seconds": 195.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.08,
      "end_seconds": 201.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Two months now. I take tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.86,
      "end_seconds": 207.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.41,
      "end_seconds": 211.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.03,
      "end_seconds": 215.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.31,
      "end_seconds": 219.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.88,
      "end_seconds": 222.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.74,
      "end_seconds": 228.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.39,
      "end_seconds": 232.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.01,
      "end_seconds": 237.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.46,
      "end_seconds": 242.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.54,
      "end_seconds": 249.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid, for about ten years. Yes, gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.54,
      "end_seconds": 251.44,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.27,
      "end_seconds": 257.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.11,
      "end_seconds": 260.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.12,
      "end_seconds": 266.23,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Right, I've had an enlarged prostate for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.06,
      "end_seconds": 269.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.57,
      "end_seconds": 277.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Alright, an underactive thyroid and heart disease, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.08,
      "end_seconds": 285.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.49,
      "end_seconds": 289.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Right, I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.9,
      "end_seconds": 309.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Tapping over the wrist brings on the tingling and the thumb muscle is slightly thin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.85,
      "end_seconds": 322.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Let's book a nerve conduction study to look into carpal tunnel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 323.58,
      "end_seconds": 326.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "The earliest is Monday, 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.47,
      "end_seconds": 340.54,
      "duration_seconds": 13.07,
      "text": "Wear a wrist splint at night. I'm going to send a referral to the hand clinic. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.05,
      "end_seconds": 347.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.62,
      "end_seconds": 351.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}